    "rationale": "KCNN4 encodes the calcium-activated Gardos potassium channel. Gain-of-function variants increase potassium efflux from erythrocytes, with accompanying salt and water loss that dehydrates the cells and produces hereditary xerocytosis/dehydrated hereditary stomatocytosis. Strongest alternative resolved: PIEZO1 is a common cause of hereditary xerocytosis and would be a reasonable phenotype-level alternative, but pathogenic PIEZO1 variants are excluded and functional testing directly demonstrates excessive calcium-activated potassium efflux, localizing the defect to the KCNN4 Gardos channel."
